# Build context uploaded by `gcloud run deploy/jobs deploy --source=.`
# (infra/builder.deploy.sh, infra/builder-job.deploy.sh).
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads the entire working tree — 1.8GB here, which
# stalls the deploy long before Cloud Build ever starts. Note that
# .dockerignore does NOT help: it is applied by the builder, after the upload.
#
# Keep in mind these are different filters with different jobs:
#   .gcloudignore  — what gets UPLOADED to Cloud Build
#   .dockerignore  — what gets into the IMAGE from what was uploaded
# Anything the Dockerfile COPYs must survive both. Today that is services/,
# agent/system-prompt.md and agent/skills/check.py.

.git/
.github/
.claude/

# Local Python env + caches — never a build input.
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Local scanner artifacts (data/downloads, scanner.db) and scratch space.
data/
tmp/

# Model-eval snapshots: local-only and gitignored because agent output embeds
# raw dataset content including personal contact details. The builder
# Dockerfile COPYs services/page_builder wholesale, so without this line
# (and the matching one in .dockerignore) every --source deploy would bake
# that PII into the image.
services/page_builder/harness-comparison/

# Node/Nuxt build products. frontend/ SOURCE is kept: the legacy
# cloudbuild-publish.yaml path builds the publisher image from it.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.output/
frontend/.nuxt/
node_modules/

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
*.db
